Hi Everyone,

I've updated the welcome message with the process for applying to Linux=20
Kernel project via Outreachy's new website.

Please check it and feel free to ask us any questions.

On Monday, February 12, 2018 at 12:30:40 AM UTC+5:30, Vaishali Thakkar=20
wrote:
>
> Greetings potential Linux kernel Outreachy interns!
>
> Please read this *entire* email, even if you have applied in the past.
>
>
> What is Outreachy?
> -------------------------
>
> The next application round for Outreachy internships starts tomorrow,
> February 12 and ends March 22.  Outreachy interns are paid $5,500
> to work on a full-time internship with an open source mentor from
> May, 2018 to August, 2018. Interns are also granted a $500 travel
> stipend to go to any conference approved by their mentor that relates
> to their project.
>
> Who can apply?
> ---------------------
>
> To qualify to apply for Outreachy, you must meet the following
> requirements:
>
> * You must be over 18 by May 30, 2018,
> * You must be able to work full-time (40 hours per week) from May 30,
> 2018 to August 30, 2018,
> * You are available for a full-time, 40 hours a week internship from May
> 30, 2018 to August 30, 2018
>
> * You are a resident or national of any country or region other than
> Crimea, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, or Syria. Note that United States
> permanent residents are eligible regardless of their nation of origin
> citizenship. Nationals of Crimea, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, or Syria who
> are permanent residents of another country should contact the Outreachy
> Organizers to determine eligibility.
>
> * You are not a person or entity restricted by US export controls or
> sanctions programs
>
> * You are eligible to work in the country or countries in which you will
> reside throughout the duration of the program
>
> * You will not have another full-time job for at least seven weeks betwee=
n
> May 30, 2018 to August 30, 2018. Having a job that is more than 20 hours
> a week is considered a full-time job commitment.
>
>
> Please check the complete eligibility criteria here:
> https://www.outreachy.org/apply/eligibility/ and contact the Outreachy
> organizers (https://www.outreachy.org/contact/organizers/) if you will be=
=20
> in
> school between May 30, 2018 and August 30, 2018 and have any
> questions about your eligibility.
>
> What Outreachy projects can you apply to?
> ---------------------------------------------------------
>
> There will be several different open source projects participating
> in this round of Outreachy. The full list can be found here:
>
> https://www.outreachy.org/communities/cfp/
>
> The Linux kernel expects to offer four projects, which are already listed
> on our wiki: http://kernelnewbies.org/OutreachyIntro and on Linux kernel
> community page on Outreachy website.
>
>
> How do I apply to the Linux kernel project?
> --------------------------------------------------------
>
> The application process for the Linux kernel project is outlined here:
> http://kernelnewbies.org/OutreachyApply
>
> Basically, applicants will need to walk through our tutorial for creating
> their first Linux kernel patch:
> http://kernelnewbies.org/Outreachyfirstpatch
>
> It is not necessary to contact a mentor before starting the tutorial.
>
> Applicants should also join the #outreachy IRC channel on irc.gnome.org,
> and the #kernel-outreachy channel on irc.oftc.net.  If you're having=20
> trouble
> with IRC, please ask for help on this mailing list.
>
> As specified in our tutorial we require Outreachy applicants to first get
> accepted at least 10 Staging driver cleanup patches. After that, we
> encourage them to move on to complete some small tasks outlined by the
> mentors. It=E2=80=99s preferable to CC the mentor when you are working on=
 the
> task so that they don=E2=80=99t miss it.
>
> The task lists for each mentor are linked from the OutreachyIntro
> page: https://kernelnewbies.org/OutreachyIntro
>
> If you=E2=80=99ve applied in the Outreachy before, you=E2=80=99re still r=
equired to send=20
> few
> staging driver cleanup patches to re-familiarize yourself with the proces=
s
> before you start to work on tasks.
>
> *Before* you start on a task, please claim that task through this page,
> unless the task explicitly states that this is not necessary:
>
> http://kernelnewbies.org/OutreachyTasks
>
> There is a tips section at the end of the tutorial to outline what
> behaviors we look for in potential Outreachy interns.  I hope this will
> give more insight into our selection process.
>
> *Please note* that from this round, you are required to fill out the
> application on the Outreachy website at the beginning of the application
> process.
>
> All the best!
>
> ---
> Vaishali Thakkar
> Outreachy Linux Kernel Co-coordinator
>

